PART 1. Witness = 'first two digits equal' (two columns, f = 2).  comm(g) = rank of [g(x)g, Pi].
 m=1 q=2: all 4 free generators commute with the witness: True; a random permutation of the digit and a random diagonal also: True
   blocks of rank k=1: 1 independent tuples tried; (rank mod p1, rank mod p2): count = {(2, 2): 1}; predicted 2(q - 2^(m-k)) = 2
   kernel K: [2, 2]; predicted 2(q-1) = 2
   free * move * free: [2, 2] (same as one move: 2)
